From 61e3ace8d27aaff3ee837ce6c38300c825425ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juniorverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:51:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] media: qcom: camss: carry the PHY type and convert
 C-PHY link rates

CAMSS only knows D-PHY links. Prepare the common code for C-PHY without
changing D-PHY behaviour.

Add a cphy flag to the CSIPHY lane configuration and to the CSID PHY
configuration, and pass it to camss_get_link_freq().

V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ is defined as 1 / (2 * UI). On C-PHY the UI is one
symbol time, so the symbol rate is twice the link frequency, and one
trio carries 16 bits in 7 symbols, which is 2.28 bits per symbol. When a
sensor offers only a pixel rate, derive the link frequency with that
factor (57/25) instead of the one bit per UI of D-PHY.

The CSIPHY and CSID clock rates are derived from the bit rate of a lane.
Add camss_get_bit_clock(), which scales a C-PHY link frequency to the
D-PHY link frequency that carries the same number of bits, and use it
for both clock calculations. For D-PHY it returns the link frequency
unchanged.

Nothing sets the flag yet: the endpoint parser still rejects C-PHY.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
